We define the \emph{Schwartz space} $\mathcal{S}$ via
\begin{align*}
    \mathcal{S} = \left\{\phi\in C^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})\mid \forall \bm{\alpha}, \forall N\in \mathbb{N},\;\sup_{\mathbf x\in \mathbb{R}^{d}}\left|(1+|\mathbf x|)^{N}D^{\bm{\alpha}}\phi(\mathbf x)\right| < \infty\right\}.
\end{align*}
We say that a sequence $\{\phi_j\}^{\infty}_{j=1}\subset \mathcal{S}$ tends to zero iff
\begin{align*}
    \sup_{\mathbf x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}|(1+|\mathbf x|)^{N}D^{\bm{\alpha}}\phi_j(\mathbf x)|\to 0 
\end{align*}
