\label{defi:cont_embed}
    A Hilbert space $(X,\|\cdot\|)$ is said to continuously embed into Hilbert space $(Y,\|\cdot\|)$ if $X\subset Y$ and there exists a constant $C$ such that $\|x\|_{Y}\leq C\|x\|_{X} $ for all $x\in X$. 
    We denote this as $X\hookrightarrow Y$. The embedding norm $\|X\hookrightarrow Y\|$ is defined as the smallest constant $C$ for which the above inequality holds.

\label{def:interpolation_space}
